 {r}←installFolder CheckForDowngrades tempDir;oldFilename;newFilename;oldIDs;newIDs;ind;i;offenders;msg
⍝ Throws an error when replacing the packages in `installFolder` by the ones just installed into
⍝ `tempDir` would bring in an *earlier* version of a package that is already installed.\\
⍝ `ReInstallDependencies_` widens an exact version to its major version line when `update` is 1, so
⍝ whatever a Registry offers as the best version of that line is what gets installed - even when
⍝ that is older than what is there already. That is what happens to a version that was withdrawn
⍝ from the Registry it came from, or that was never published in the first place. Because the
⍝ install folder is then swapped for the temporary one, the only copy there is would be gone.\\
⍝ Packages are matched by their major version line, so an update to a later major version is not a
⍝ downgrade: the old line simply has no counterpart in the new build list.\\
⍝ Without a build list on either side there is nothing to compare, and nothing is done.
 r←0
 oldFilename←(F.AddTrailingSep installFolder),Reg.BuildListFilename
 newFilename←(F.AddTrailingSep tempDir),Reg.BuildListFilename
 :If F.IsFile oldFilename
 :AndIf F.IsFile newFilename
     oldIDs←,⊆(Reg.JSON⊃F.NGET oldFilename).packageID
     newIDs←,⊆(Reg.JSON⊃F.NGET newFilename).packageID
     ind←(Reg.RemoveMinorAndPatch¨oldIDs)⍳Reg.RemoveMinorAndPatch¨newIDs
     offenders←''
     :For i :In ⍳≢newIDs
         :If (i⊃ind)≤≢oldIDs
         :AndIf ((i⊃ind)⊃oldIDs)Reg.IsLaterThan(i⊃newIDs)
             offenders,←⊂((i⊃ind)⊃oldIDs)(i⊃newIDs)
         :EndIf
     :EndFor
     :If 0<≢offenders
         msg←'Refused: this would replace ',(⍕≢offenders),' installed package'
         msg,←((1<≢offenders)/'s'),' by an earlier version:'
         msg,←⊃,/{CR,'  ',(1⊃⍵),'  -->  ',2⊃⍵}¨offenders
         msg,←CR,'Re-install without "update", or publish the installed version first.'
         msg Assert 0
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
⍝Done
